[COMMENTS]
STATION,Structure utilising the fall of an old navigation lock, gauging a rural catchment with sand, gravel, and loam, some flow bypasses the station through a marsh u/s of station. GENERAL: Crump type weir utilising the fall of an old navigation lock. No chart back up: limited space within kiosk. STATION HYDROMETRY: One rating applied across period of record. FLOW RECORD: Logger failure Jan 1998 so no DMFs. Suspect data in summer 1996. Pre-digital data peak flow data are rejected as stage cannot be reprocessed following a datum change pre-1992. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8). No data between 17 May 2019 to 3 July 2019 due to due to weir works to restore upstream levels. FLOW REGIME: Groundwater abstractions for public water supply moderately reduce the natural runoff.
CATCHMENT,Predominantly rural catchment of approximately half sand and gravel and half loam. Immediately u/s is a large marshy area with dense weed growth from which some flow bypasses the station.
Qmed Suitability,Gaugings support rating close to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Rating cannot be confirmed for high flows.
[END]
